module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.LogIdealAlgebraizationData

/-!
# LogIdealImageChartFormula

A step of logarithmic image-ideal algebraization.
(blueprint: lem-trf-log-ideal-image-chart-formula).
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Any ideal algebraizing the structural image has the inclusion-normalized
finite-chart formula. Source: ILO, Exposé VIII 3.3.7 and 3.4.2; Stacks, Tags
01IB, 03DV and 0GN7 (blueprint: lem-trf-log-ideal-image-chart-formula).

Proof: Fix an affine étale fine chart and finite nonempty generators E as in
the conclusion. The chart-generation equality at every geometric stalk shows
that the structural image ideal is generated by the functions alpha(e): every
ideal germ is e*m and alpha is multiplicative, while the generators themselves
belong to the ideal stalk. In the strict local ring at any geometric point of
the chart, the same equality describes the image of the tilde ideal generated
by these functions. Thus the associated tilde inclusion and the restriction
of the algebraized ideal have the same image at every geometric stalk.
Étale tensor pullback is flat, so both inclusions are monic. Their small-étale
image subobjects therefore agree. Full faithfulness of étale association
lifts their inclusion-preserving isomorphism to the unique Zariski module
isomorphism on Spec A. The affine tilde/Gamma counit identifies the tilde
inclusion with the displayed subtype map composed with tildeSelf; naturality
fixes its normalization. For two such isomorphisms, cancel this monic tilde
inclusion to identify their hom maps, and hence the isomorphisms. The argument
allows alpha(e) = 0, a unit among the generators, and the zero affine ring. -/
theorem logIdeal_image_chart_formula {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : EtaleLogStructure X)
    (I : M.IdealFamily) (K : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hK : M.IsImageIdealAlgebraization I K) : M.HasImageIdealChartFormula I K := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
